            0.713,
            0.85,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Such methods of applying the distributive property to easily multiply two numbers were discussed extensively in the ancient mathematical works of Brahmagupta (628 CE), Sridharacharya (750 CE) and Bhaskaracharya (Lilavati, 1150 CE). In his work Brahmasphuṭasiddhānta (Verse 12.56), Brahmagupta refers to such methods for fast multiplication using the distributive property as "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "ista-gunana.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
